INT. ST. BRIDGET'S CHURCH BASEMENT - NIGHT

MONTAGE - FOLDING CHAIRS, STYROFOAM CUPS, A BANNER THAT SAYS "ONE DAY AT A TIME" WITH THE "ONE" PEELING OFF

KIM HALLORAN
(slamming a coffee pot onto the table, steam rising)
I am telling you, the sober cake is not a cake, it is a loaf, and I will not be lied to about baked goods in a house of God.

KIP HALLORAN
(sitting in the circle, raising one finger like a student)
Technically we're in the basement.

MR. DELACROIX
(rubbing his eyes under his glasses)
Technically we are all in the basement.

This is the loudest this room has been all year.

KIM HALLORAN
(pointing at Kip with a stir stick)
You promised me, Kip. You said no more texts to the ex.

ON PHONE: "KIP: just checking in. hope u are well"

KIP HALLORAN
(hiding the phone under his thigh)
That's not me. That's a different Kip.

SISTER AGNES
(from the folding table, arranging donuts into a perfect spiral)
There is only one Kip, and the Lord has seen your thumbs.

BIG TOMASZ
(raising his hand slowly, standing, sitting back down, standing again)
Can I say something? I only came for the donuts, and I am now somehow crying, and that is Kip's fault.

KIM HALLORAN
(softening, setting down the stir stick)
Oh, Tomasz.

MR. DELACROIX
(clapping once, bright)
Okay! Deep breaths. In through the nose. Out through the donut.

SISTER AGNES
(offering the plate around the circle)
Take one. They are not a sacrament.

KIP HALLORAN
(taking two, handing one to Kim)
Truce?

KIM HALLORAN
(biting into it, rolling her eyes)
Truce. But the loaf thing stands.

SMASH CUT TO:

INT. ST. BRIDGET'S CHURCH BASEMENT - LATER

The chairs are stacked. The banner finally falls.
